{"name":"Ash","hex":"#bebaa7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Ash","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Egyptian god of oases.","Oisc, also spelled Æsc or Ash, an Anglo-Saxon king of Kent"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ash"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ash","blocks":[{"text":"Ash is the solid remnants of fires. Specifically, ash refers to all non-aqueous, non-gaseous residues that remain after something burns. In analytical chemistry, to analyse the mineral and metal content of chemical samples, ash is the non-gaseous, non-liquid residue after complete combustion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Wood_ash.jpg/330px-Wood_ash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ash","wikidata":"Q152079"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/500px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/1280px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/500px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAir_pollution3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/HK_Sheung_Wan_Wing_Lok_Street_fire_burning_offering_papers_Chinese_style_December_2018_IX2_02.jpg/500px-HK_Sheung_Wan_Wing_Lok_Street_fire_burning_offering_papers_Chinese_style_December_2018_IX2_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/HK_Sheung_Wan_Wing_Lok_Street_fire_burning_offering_papers_Chinese_style_December_2018_IX2_02.jpg/1280px-HK_S